        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            On a plain concrete driveway in a cold, salted climate, buy a silane-siloxane penetrating sealer and get it down before the first frost. Ghostshield Siloxa-Tek 8500 leads for heavy salt exposure, Foundation Armor SX5000 WB is the simplest ready-to-use choice, and Eagle Natural Seal suits a tight budget. On an older, dusty slab, densify with a lithium silicate first and put the repellent on afterward.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Save film sealers for decorative concrete, and accept the recoats and grit additive that come with them. Then keep up the small habits each year: keep joints filled, go easy on deicers, never use ammonium-based products, and test with water every fall. Those habits add years to a driveway.
          </p>
